In article <652a1k$lqk$1@news.doit.wisc.edu>,
Tingli Pan <tpan@norman.ssc.wisc.edu> wrote:
>Is there a way to read tape in VMS system from Digital unix? The VMS
>version is 6.2 with Multinet 4.0. The Digital unix system is 3.2. The
>tape can be in any format for the VMS system.

If the data to be transferred is a lot of small files - possibly
spanning several directory trees - the most
convenient way to do this is VMSTAR.  Then you just use tar on the
DU box to read the tape.  Most text, and some binary, files will
be properly transferred by this method.  RMS Indexed files (i.e. MAIL.MAI,
etc.) files will almost certainly get scrambled.

If there's one enormous file of, say, binary data, it may be more
convenient and efficient to MOUNT/FOR the tape under VMS with an
appropriate blocksize, COPY the file to the tape under VMS, and
read it on the Unix box with "dd".

Tim. (shoppa@triumf.ca)



