>I have a Digital DEC2000 installed with osf/1 ver 3.2.  The system has users log in 24 hrs a day, nonstop.  I need to find a way to stop users from coming in so that I can do backup.  Apart from modify the /etc/inittab and run 'init q'; i s there anyway to stop new users coming in?  Also when existing user logout the connection is closed to prevent others from seizing the connection.  Most of my users connect to the machine remotely by lat.  Anyone can help?
>
