In article <34730CF3.4DCC@psipenta.com> roofus <jroof@psipenta.com> writes:
>Eric COISSAC wrote:
>> I unfortunatly deleted the generic kernel file /genvmunix on an osf1
>> server. Is it possible copy this file from an other server.
>
>i think you can do an other way.
>there is in /sys/conf a file GENERIC.
>do doconfic - c GENERIC should bring you genvmunix back


Don't do this. GENERIC does not always build on a system (you need
all optional subsets installed), and doesn't quite produce genvmunix
anyway; you need to ostrip -x the file first.

You can get genvmunix off of any other system running the same O/S
release, or off the installation media as /vmunix.

However, unless you plan on adding hardware and building new kernels
to use it, you don't need genvmunix at all.

