|> Hi All !
|> 
|> Is there a way to know the date when a file was created?

Not under Unix - come back MVS, all is forgiven :-)  Well, perhaps
not, at least in this context ....

There are several things for which it would be very useful to know
when the inode was allocated (i.e. the file was 'created'), but the
information is not stored.  There is some evidence that struct stat
ctime field was originally intended to be the creation timestamp,
but it has been used for the inode change timestamp since the early
days of Unix.


