This is bug #518917.

The NIS client code has an historical limit of 1600 bytes on any 
NIS request, so ypwhich fails to decode any packet larger than that.

You'd need to built a libc which uses (fe.)4096 byte buffers for NIS 
requests. This increases the yp buffer size to 4096. None of the 
getXbyY calls use this code any longer so this will only have an 
effect on applications which directly use the yp library routines.


