Nikola Milutinovic wrote:
> 
> willig.reimund@gdr.de wrote:
> >
> > Hallo ,
> > does anyone know which kind of file-system the original DUNIX
> > operatimng system cd-rom uses. We would like to distribut some
> > programs for a large number of DUNIX-Servers, so burning a cd-rom
> > would be nice. But which format should we use?
> 
> UFS BSD 4.4 I think.
> 
> Nix.

Correct, it is the UFS file system.  The one advantage of going with UFS
is that you know every Digital UNIX system can read it.  However, you
won't be able to read it on other types of systems.

The alternative is to use the ISO 9660 format.  I believe that all newer
versions of Digital UNIX (V4.0 & later) have support for this format
enabled by default.  Older versions also support it but may require a
kernel build to add support since it wasn't enabled by default.  An
advantage of this format is the ability to read the CDROM on non-Digital
UNIX systems.

I hope this was hopeful.

Dave
