Ong Liang Bu (onglb@NIEVAX.NIE.AC.SG) wrote:
> I have a Digital DEC2000 installed with osf/1 ver 3.2.  The system
> has users log in 24 hrs a day, nonstop.  I need to find a way to
> stop users from coming in so that I can do backup.  Apart from
> modify the /etc/inittab and run 'init q'; i s there anyway to stop
> new users coming in?  Also when existing user logout the connection
> is closed to prevent others from seizing the connection.  Most of my
> users connect to the machine remotely by lat.  Anyone can help?

If you have C2 security, you can restrict when users can login to
system.  For example, with edauth command you can add something like
"u_tod=Any0800-2000", which will allow user to login any day between
8am and 8pm.

If you don't have C2 enabled, you can just touch /etc/nologin, do
backup, and then remove /etc/nologin.

