In article <65am3t$svg$1@power42t.hkbu.edu.hk>, s11976@net2.hkbu.edu.hk (Pui Ming WONG) writes:

>How do i find out the default block size of files written to
>my tape device (say /dev/rmt0h) ?

See what the particular command uses as a default.  There isn't
an operating system default for the tape block sizes as different
applications see them.  The particular command will typically have
