In article <EK5uD9.BrL.A.ebony@news.trentu.ca>, clos@ivory.trentu.ca writes:
|> I would like to know the best way to display *all* currently
|> active Kernel values. Is "sysconfig -q " the best command for this?
|> I am  running DU version 3.2C.

I've used this csh script:

	foreach subsys (`/sbin/sysconfig -s | sed 's/:.*//'`)
	/sbin/sysconfig -q $subsys | grep -v ':' | sed "s/.*/$subsys"": &/"
	end

no guarantees!

