Brian O'Neill wrote:

> ... is there a corresponding one [Xsession file] for CDE?

Yes. The custom Xsession file is located in /etc/dt/config/Xsession.
Unless you've done any customization of your system, the path probably
doesn't exist. dtlogin(1) says that the default file should be copied
from /usr/dt/bin/Xsession (that's BIN) to /etc/dt/config/Xsession
(that's CONFIG). Or you could take the easy way out and drop something
into  /etc/dt/config/Xsession.d/. Here, we use /etc/.../Xsession.d/ to
set up search paths to our application host. But if you're launching an
X application, you'll need to muck with Xsession itself.
(/etc/.../Xsession.d/ launches before dthello).

Read dtlogin(1) for the execution stages of Xsession. I've been burned
there before...



