A short quiz for anyone interested.

Spot the "deliberate" mistake in the example STREAMS module given
in Annex A of the DEC UNIX Network Programmer's Guide (essentially
unchanged, I think, since OSF/1 v 2.0).

Hint..... Write a program which pushes the module on a STREAM 
(e.g a fifo/named pipe) and sends some data around it. Run it and 
terminate the process (e.g. with a signal) _without_ close()ing
the file descriptors. On OSF 3.2g (and other DU versions I 
suspect), make sure that you've saved any data/edits, etc and don't
care about getting grief from other users because you've just 
been forced to hit the reset switch and reboot.

Answers on a posting........

