> options : java enabled etc... OK. but applets are not running...
> 
> Is there any problem with libraries ?... Because I found on the net only
> netscape for OSF 3.2...

Yes, there is.  If you are using netscape that came with OS, then
netscape executable should be shell script that "preloads" old libXt
library (usualy located in same directory as netscape and
real-netscape, check path in netscape shell script), and then starts
program real-netscape.

Now, when you install new version of netscape, you should make similar
setup.  Put real netscape executable in file called real-netscape,
copy netscape shell script and old libXt.so that came with system in
same directory as real-netscape, and after that java should run.

