From: berkley@kite.cs.wustl.edu (Berkley Shands)
Subject: NT -> OSF alpha u-code
Date: 1997/11/14
Message-ID: <64hsk6$a31@kite.cs.wustl.edu>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 289537145
Organization: Washington University, St. Louis MO
Newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1




To change over to OSF from NT, you must first re-write the ARM console u-code
into SRM console u-code. (You can go back if needed). You MUST have a digitial
supported graphics card (Not MATROX) if you want to have anything other than
VGA graphics on the workstation head. If you want this to be a server, then
that's no problem :-) right?

First you need to access the firmware site:
ftp://ftp.digital.com/pub/Digital/Alpha/firmware/index.html
ftp://ftp.digital.com/pub/Digital/Alpha/firmware/readmes/dpw433.html

Be SURE you read all the documentation before you start changing u-code!
Download the files and make the floppy(s) you need. 
Follow the menus to update the firmware. (you will do this TWICE).
The NT box will figure out you want to load the SRM code, then power fail
the box. You are now ready to setup the console to use OSF. Set the
ewa0 selection, and the boot flags.  Go for it.

To get back to NT (Oh, NO! Mr. Bill!!!) use the ARM floppy and update the
u-code.  Just as the doc says, enter "fwupdate.exe" and it will go back.
It took me the better part of a day to download all the files and get the
proceedure right only to find that the matrox cards are unsupported.

Berkley Shands, a very satisfied 433au owner.
Department of Computer Science




