We run a Alpha System 1000 with 6 X 2 Gb SCSI discs on a SWXCR_EB 3 channel
RAID controller, configured as a single array group at RAID level 5.
A TLZ07 DAT tape drive is attached to the same SCSI controller.
The OS is OSF1 V3.0     358.78

We run a full backup to the tape every night using vdump, it takes over 3
hours..

Monday night the back up completes as normal with no errors.
Tuesday the system reports that it cannot write to the media, so we put in
a new tape for the backup on Wednesday.
Wednesday's backup fails and we cannot get the tape out.
	OK 2 failed backups but we have RAID!
Thursday on the advice of DEC we need to take down the system to replace
the defective tape unit. It is shut down normally at the end a work on
Thursday.

The tape drive is replaced the system is booted and it cannot find the
ADVFS.
	Panic! the engineer says that the hardware is OK but we need to rebuild
the system from a backup, there is no software to retrieve the information
relating to the RAID array and what is on it.

The sytem was rebuild OK according to instructions but to add to our
problems the tape from Monday nights backup will not read to the point
where our most essential data is and again there is no software to get
passed a bad block of tape if this is the problem. so it back to Sunday.

What did we do wrong?

We took advice from DEC on the configuration and set up and had someone
trained by DEC.


Is RAID a big con trick?

Why sell tape drives which cannot tell whether data has been correctly
stored.


Angry IT Manager





