>Hello,

>I have some 2Gb DEC fast wide SCSI disk in StorageWorks canisters,
>currently installed in a AlphaServer 2100, running Digital UNIX 4.0b.

>I was think about installing some on a Ultra Enterprise 1, using a
>SunSwift SBus card or similar, Solaris 2.5.x-2.6.

>Has anyone out there attempt something similar?  Success?  Problems
>with disk firmware?

Should work OK, but be aware that the DEC-onbase (so, intended for
use on Digital machines) drives are normally set to wait for a SCSI
spinup command. Check out gatekeeper.dec.com, it should have the
RZspinup tool somewhere.

The SWX labeled disks are intended for multivendor use and are set
for staggered spinup, that is wait xx seconds times the SCSI ID.
The SWX are also the ones really *supported* for use on Sun boxes.

Wilko

