>nslookup is able to resolve names to IP numbers. But unfortunately,
>when I try to telnet to the same names that were resolved by nslookup,
>I am told it is an unknown host. 

Check to see if the IP addresses match in NIS and DNS.  Maybe they don't.
telnet, ping, and ftp use gethostbyname() which may be set to resolve
via NIS before DNS.  On Solaris, check the hosts line in /etc/nsswitch.conf.
If this is SunOS, you'll have to check the FAQ to setup the shared library
libc.so to use DNS rather than NIS.

Good luck,

