The file system full condition may be encountered where there
is actually file space available but the ADVfs filesystem has
run out of BMT extents due to fragementation. This is roughly
equivalent to running out of inodes. If you are running ADVfs,
look at the -x and -p switches to mkfdmn and use approp values
to avoid premature file system full problems.

This is most often encountered on filesystems with high create/delete
rates with many small files, as in mail and news spool.

