at any time, just so you know.  I would have suggested using MRU, if
it weren't for the fact they don't list exb-10i jukeboxes in their
SPD.  You can always use the CLC kit if you license another product
that uses it.  MRU (Media Robot Utility) and NetWorker are two products
which use CLC.  MRU is not expensive but NetWorker may cover your need
for the product.  Or... you could write your own driver, but if I recall
correctly, the engineers here had more exceptions to the specs with
exabyte jukeboxes than they ever wanted to see again.  The 8mm drive/tapes
prior to ait drives are really awful though.  Don't let anyone put data
that really matters on those.  (Speaking as someone who still has an
exb-10e hooked up to my nt box, I know not to depend on old type 8mm tapes).

