PS and VMSTAT do not use the kernel name list.

Some things that likely won't work: crash dumps. dbx -k. kloadsrv
(loadable drivers). netstat. nfsstat. route. arp. rarpd. pfstat.
strsetup. trpt.


Let me repeat my original statement:

Stripping the kernel has absolutely no effect on available memory, or
system performance. The only thing it will do is stop some utilities
and daemons from running (which may help performance since they are
not there....)

