It is the operating system disk image.  You would have found this bit
of information in the hier(5) manual page.  Since you're in the
neighborhood, the file genvmunix is a kernel with drivers for all
supported device built in to it.  Genvmunix can be booted on any
system supported by its version.

Many program use the kernel symbol table to wander around through
kernel memory to get interesting bits of information from those
data structures that don't support a callable interface.
