nilesh@cdac.ernet.in wants to know how to boot his DEC Unix
machine into single-user mode with write access to the disks.
This works on my AlphaServer 1000 running DUNIX 3.2d:

From the console prompt (>>>), issue this boot command
     boot -flag s
This will boot into single user mode.  Then, when you get
the single-user mode shell prompt (#), issue this command
to check the disks and mount all filesystems:
     bcheckrc

