> 
> Are there any experts around who could give us pointers about what to 
> attempt to restore (at least parts) of the data? Thanks for your help!!

     There is nothing much you can do but to rmfdmn <domain> and
     mkfdmn all over again and restore files from backup. Tools to
     correct and maintain advfs are mildly put nonexistant. And when they
     are corrupted your machine panics and nothing points to ADVFS.. 

     In my opinion ADVFS is load of shit and should not be used to hold
     anything valuable. I have restored my 50+ GB ADVFS three times from
     scratch, and I'm not going to do it again. I've ordered a RAID-array
     and switching to UFS as soon as possible.

